import ../../../ui/scene_orbit.dl
import ../../../ui/appearance.dl

to [expect orbit vector] {vector:actual} [near] {vector:expected}:
    require condition ((the length of (actual - expected)) < 0.000001) reporting "An orbit camera moved to the wrong world position"

set origin to a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.0,0.0]
set camera to a UI scene camera at (a UI scene vector from [0.0,4.0,10.0]) aimed at origin with angle 35.0 aspect 1.0 near 0.1 far 1000.0
set orbit to a UI scene orbit for camera between distances 2.0 and 100.0 and polar angles 0.05 and 1.5
expect orbit vector (orbit's camera's position) near (camera's position)
require condition ((UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) is moving) = false) reporting "A new orbit camera started animating without input"
turn UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by yaw 1.5707963267948966 polar 0.0
require condition (UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) is moving) reporting "Orbit input did not schedule motion"
require condition (advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 10.0 seconds) reporting "Orbit input did not move the camera"
expect orbit vector (orbit's camera's position) near (a UI scene vector from [10.0,4.0,0.0])
require condition ((advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 0.1 seconds) = false) reporting "A settled orbit kept requesting frames"

# Damping must depend on elapsed time, rather than the number of drawn frames.
set first to a UI scene orbit for camera between distances 2.0 and 100.0 and polar angles 0.05 and 1.5
set second to first
turn UI scene orbit (the address of first) by yaw 0.7 polar -0.3
turn UI scene orbit (the address of second) by yaw 0.7 polar -0.3
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of first) by 0.2 seconds
loop index from 0 to 20:
    set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of second) by 0.01 seconds
expect orbit vector (first's camera's position) near (second's camera's position)

focus UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) on (a UI scene vector from [10.0,0.0,0.0]) viewed from (a UI scene vector from [10.0,4.0,-10.0]) over 0.65 seconds
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 0.325 seconds
expect orbit vector (orbit's camera's target) near (a UI scene vector from [5.0,0.0,0.0])
require condition ((the length of (orbit's camera's position - orbit's camera's target)) > 10.0) reporting "A focus animation crossed through its target"
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 0.325 seconds
expect orbit vector (orbit's camera's position) near (a UI scene vector from [10.0,4.0,-10.0])
require condition ((UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) is moving) = false) reporting "A completed focus animation kept requesting frames"

zoom UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by factor 0.0001
turn UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by yaw 0.0 polar -100.0
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 10.0 seconds
require condition ((orbit's distance = 2.0) and (orbit's polar = 0.05)) reporting "Orbit zoom and pitch ignored their limits"
pan UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by (a UI scene vector from [1.0,2.0,3.0])
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of orbit) by 10.0 seconds
expect orbit vector (orbit's camera's target) near (a UI scene vector from [11.0,2.0,3.0])

# Camera-up is an axis, not an assumption that every scene uses world Y.
set camera's position to a UI scene vector from [0.0,10.0,4.0]
set camera's up to a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.0,1.0]
set tilted to a UI scene orbit for camera between distances 2.0 and 100.0 and polar angles 0.05 and 1.5
turn UI scene orbit (the address of tilted) by yaw 1.5707963267948966 polar 0.0
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of tilted) by 10.0 seconds
expect orbit vector (tilted's camera's position) near (a UI scene vector from [-10.0,0.0,4.0])

set camera's up to a UI scene vector from [0.0,1.0,0.0]
set camera's position to a UI scene vector from [0.01,4.0,-10.0]
set wrapped to a UI scene orbit for camera between distances 2.0 and 100.0 and polar angles 0.05 and 1.5
turn UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) by yaw 0.02 polar 0.0
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) by 0.01 seconds
require condition (wrapped's camera's position's z < -9.9) reporting "Crossing the yaw boundary spun the camera around the long route"
focus UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) on origin viewed from (a UI scene vector from [0.0,4.0,10.0]) over 0.0 seconds
expect orbit vector (wrapped's camera's position) near (a UI scene vector from [0.0,4.0,10.0])
require condition ((UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) is moving) = false) reporting "Instant focus scheduled an animation"
focus UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) on (a UI scene vector from [50.0,0.0,0.0]) viewed from (a UI scene vector from [50.0,5.0,10.0]) over 1.0 seconds
set changed to advance UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) by 0.25 seconds
set previous to wrapped's camera's position
turn UI scene orbit (the address of wrapped) by yaw 0.1 polar 0.0
expect orbit vector (wrapped's camera's position) near previous
require condition (wrapped's duration = 0.0) reporting "Manual orbit did not cancel programmatic focus"

set bounds to @intrinsic("construct", UI mesh bounds, a UI scene vector from [-10.0,-0.5,-10.0], a UI scene vector from [10.0,2.0,10.0])
set target to a UI scene vector from [0.0,0.4,0.0]
set direction to (a UI scene vector from [0.48,0.73,0.60]) normalized
set camera to a UI scene camera at (target + direction) aimed at target with angle 35.0 aspect 1.0 near 0.1 far 1000.0
for each aspect in [1.77777777777778,1.0,0.5625,0.2,4.0]:
    set camera's aspect to aspect
    set distance to the distance framing UI scene bounds bounds through camera within horizontal 0.96 vertical 0.86
    set camera's position to target + direction * distance
    set viewport to UI box at 0.0 0.0 sized (500.0 * aspect) 500.0
    for each x in [-10.0,10.0]:
        for each y in [-0.5,2.0]:
            for each z in [-10.0,10.0]:
                set projected to the UI scene projection for (a UI scene vector from [x,y,z]) through camera in viewport
                require condition (projected's visible) reporting "Resizing clipped a corner of the framed scene"
                set horizontal to ((projected's screen's x / viewport's width) * 2.0) - 1.0
                set vertical to ((projected's screen's y / viewport's height) * 2.0) - 1.0
                require condition (((the absolute value of horizontal) <= 0.96001) and ((the absolute value of vertical) <= 0.86001)) reporting "Scene framing did not preserve its viewport margins"
print line "Scene cameras orbit, zoom, pan and focus smoothly with elapsed-time damping, arbitrary up axes, settled-frame detection and responsive bounds framing."
